# Build output.
/target
# Packaged test builds from `docs/package.ps1`: the staging folder and the
# zip are ignored, but the installer is committed, so the newest build is
# always one click away for someone who only wants the .exe. (At ~50 MB each,
# every version kept adds to the clone; GitHub Releases is the lighter home.)
/dist/*
!/dist/*-setup.exe
# The Milestone 0 spike is outside the workspace, so it has its own target dir.
/spike/*/target

# The FFmpeg SDK: ~250 MB of headers, import libraries and DLLs, fetched by
# `docs/fetch-ffmpeg.ps1` against a pinned hash. Never committed.
/vendor/*

# ...with one deliberate exception. `vendor/ffmpeg-binding.rs` is generated
# code, and generated code normally does not belong in a repository — but this
# file MUST be committed:
#
#   * `.cargo/config.toml` points `FFMPEG_BINDING_PATH` at it, and without it
#     `rusty_ffmpeg`'s build script falls back to bindgen and fails with
#     "Unable to find libclang".
#   * Avoiding that libclang dependency is the entire reason ADR 002 chose this
#     backend. Regenerating the file needs the LLVM toolchain that decision
#     exists to keep off contributors' machines.
#
# So a fresh clone builds after `fetch-ffmpeg.ps1` and nothing else. Deleting
# this line would break that, silently, for everyone but the person who has
# LLVM already installed.
!/vendor/ffmpeg-binding.rs

# Runtime state. `.cache/` is the proxy and thumbnail store (§67), `recovery/`
# holds crash-recovery journals (§39), and `*.vproj.tmp` is the scratch file an
# atomic save writes before renaming (§38.1). All three are regenerated, and
# none of them are the user's work.
.cache/
recovery/
*.vproj.tmp

# Editor and OS noise.
/.vscode/
/.idea/
*.iml
*.swp
*~
*.rs.bk
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
